⭐ **RESEARCH A1 is ANSWERED by this run.** The open question was whether hosted TEST's
`postgres` role bypasses `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` on `compute_job_kinds` under
`row_security = off` — the one thing the throwaway lane could not prove. The whole
transaction ran to its terminator with no RLS error and no `relation … does not exist`,
so it does. Nothing was written to find that out.

