## Why this was written late — recorded, not smoothed over

Both runs happened 2026-09-09. No `RESTORE.log` and no `SUMMARY.md` were written, so
for two days the phase had three executed plans and a fourth that looked like a pending
`checkpoint:decision`. A founder-checkpoint inventory on 2026-09-11 listed it as
requiring a founder dispatch that had, in fact, already been made.

⭐ **The inventory inferred the absence of the ACTION from the absence of the ARTIFACT.**
That inference does not hold, and it is the same shape as the reconstruction defect
`164.7-REVIEWS.md` records: rounding a record off to the shape you already believe. The
correction came from reading the two runs' job logs rather than the phase directory.

⚠️ A second error was made and corrected in the same session: the replay was first
declared ABSENT at `a622df27` on the strength of `git cat-file -e` against
`scripts/test-restore-replay-refdata.mjs` — **a filename that has never existed in this
repo**. The real files (`scripts/restore-test-refdata-allowlist.txt`,
`scripts/extract-reference-inserts.mjs`, `src/__tests__/refdata-allowlist.test.ts`)
were all present at that sha. An absence proved against a wrong name reads like a
finding and is not one. PR #767 was a HARDENING pass over the replay, not its
introduction.

⚠️ **`gh api …/actions/jobs/<id>/logs` needs `--allow-escape-sequences`** or it exits 1
with EMPTY stdout, and an empty log reads as "nothing there" (booked in
`164.7-06-SUMMARY.md`). Every reading above was taken with that flag, from logs of
1581 and 1725 lines. ⚠️ The runner ECHOES each script line prefixed with an ANSI colour
code, so a naive grep matches the SOURCE of an `echo` rather than its OUTPUT — the
first read of these logs mistook the echoed `mode=restore requires -f confirm=…` error
string for evidence of the mode. Every mode reading above comes from a line with the
echo prefix filtered OUT.
